{
  "abstract": "Quantitative Poisson approximation for long multiplicative runs requires arithmetic control uniform over growing subfamilies. The selected results give the exact affine event calculus, homogeneous and compatible-nullity envelopes, unique relation-respecting component factorization, and a weighted full-support count summed over all cardinalities with one threshold before every subset and minimum size; actual positive Hermite reference laws with an exact-parameter N^(-4/3+epsilon) upper error bound and fixed-height sharp moving total-variation equivalents; and an explicit counterexample showing that agreement at every fixed factorial-moment order, even with uniform exponential-moment control, does not imply any inverse-power total-variation rate. The quadratic positivity interval and singleton identity calibrate the positive-reference family. The counterexample is an independently constructed family of probability laws; no multiplicative realization is asserted. The selected conjunctions cover main results 2.1--2.5, 7.1 and 8.4 and companion Propositions13.1 and15.1, including the latter's displayed sequence corollary.",
